WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Good Morning Hank, it's Thursday.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.500
Special Suprise Bonus Video. So, um, I have written a book.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.000
 

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.120
That feels good to say. Also a little terrifying.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.560
It's called Turtles All the Way Down. It comes out on October 10th and it is available for preorder now.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.020
Link in the Doobly-Doo below.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.240
My previous book, The Fault in our Stars, came out more than five and a half years ago,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.740
so this book has definitely been a long and winding road,

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.400
but I am /so/ excited to share it with you.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.260
I don't want to say to much about the plot of the book

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.880
but it's a story about a young woman who's trying to solve a mystery

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.100
while also trying to live with mental illness.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.300
And in that sense, while it is definitely a made-up story,

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.960
it's also kind of a personal one

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.500
because as most of you know, I have a mental illness

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.260
that, at times, has taken over my life.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.920
So ok! I think that's all the relevant information for right now:

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.160
title, publication date, available for preorder,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.120
one sentence of extremely vague introduction!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.460
I'm so happy to be finished with the book that I'm proud of.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.060
I really hope you like it!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.560
Also, I just wanna say a quick word of thanks --

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.800
A lot of people have been /really/ patient with me

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.980
and kind over the last five and a half years,

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.940
especially my family, so...thank you!

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.060
I have often worried that I would never publish another book,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.180
and without their support, I wouldn't be.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.500
Now, I know many of you will have questions.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.880
Please leave them in comments below

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.060
and I will try to answer some in next Tuesday's video

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.580
Which, by the way, is going to be an unboxing video because I hear those are popular on YouTube.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.520
Hank, I will see you tomorrow.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.520
That's another thing I haven't gotten to say for a while.

